<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45138" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔσκοπος</span></b> , 
			Ep.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐΰσκ</span>-, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκοπέω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>keen-sighted, watchful</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐΰσκοπος Ἀργεϊφόντης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					24.24
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				7.137
			</span></i>; of Artemis, <i><span class="en">
				11.198
			</span></i> (cf. <i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>); of Heracles, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				25.143
			</span></i>; of Pan, <i><span class="en">
				Orph.
				<u>H.</u>
				11.9
			</span></i>; of men, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				11.112
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Nicarch.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>far-seen</i>, of stars and light, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ec.</u>
				2
			</span></i> (v.l.), <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.1716
			</span></i>; of places, <i>commanding a wide view</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ -ώτατα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					6.3.2
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				628a11
			</span></i> (nisi leg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐσκεπῆ</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Cat.Ma.</u>
				13
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκοπός</span>) <i>shooting well, of unerring
			aim</i> (as some explain <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				11.198
			</span></i>), of Apollo, Orac. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				5.61
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βριτόμαρτις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Dian.</u>
					190
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τόξοις πρόσωθεν εὐσκόποις χειρουμένη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ch.</u>
					694
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐσκοπώτερα βάλλειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hld.
					9.5
				</span></i>
			. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πως</span>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, βάλλειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					2.355
				</span></i>
			: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξομοιοῦν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					1.681
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐ. ἔχειν τῶν ἀποκρίσεων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>VS</u>
					2.1.9
				</span></i>
			.</div>
